Short:        Antialiased TrueType text for Workbench
Author:       Serkan Dursun
Uploader:     Serkan Dursun <EMAIL>
Type:         util/wb
Version:      0.13
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2.0
Distribution: Aminet
Requires:     68030+ or PiStorm advised (68020 works), RTG, TTF/OTF fonts

AAText makes Workbench and applications draw TrueType fonts antialiased
on RTG screens (15/16/24/32 bit): icon labels, menus, window and screen
titles, Shell windows, GadTools, ReAction and MUI programs - everything
that draws text through graphics.library.

No setup needed: every TrueType or OpenType font installed with a font manager
(fonts with a .otag file) is detected automatically and drawn smoothly
in every size, using the code page from its .otag file (Turkish,
Central European etc. work out of the box). Bitmap fonts and AGA
screens are left untouched.

Features
- Zero configuration; optional ENVARC:AAText.prefs for gamma, hinting
  (none/light/normal/full), glyph cache size, program blacklist and
  explicit font mappings
- Preferences program AATextPrefs (English and Turkish, ReAction): a
  running AAText takes every change at once, so you see it while you
  try it; Save/Use/Cancel and the usual Prefs menus
- Character sets for fonts without a code page: Latin-1 to Latin-5,
  Latin-9, Latin-10, Windows-1250, ISO-8859-5 (Cyrillic) and KOI8-R;
  AATextPrefs keeps ENV:ftcodepage (freetype2.library) in step
- "Safe" metrics by default: letters keep the cells of the system's
  bitmap font, so no window layout changes
- Optional real metrics mode ("real on"): the TrueType font's own
  character widths and pair kerning, with TextLength/TextExtent/TextFit
  kept consistent; bold, italic and underline styles supported
- Does not replace any library: patches Text(), TextLength(),
  TextExtent() and TextFit() at run time and removes them cleanly;
  start it a second time (or "AAText QUIT") to switch it off
- Fonts are rendered on AAText's own stack, so tasks with small stacks
  (input.device, Shell commands) are safe
- Versions for 68020-68040/Emu68/WinUAE and for 68060 with FPU, plus a
  debug version for bug reports

Tested on AmigaOS 3.2.3 with WinUAE (UAEGFX) and PiStorm (Emu68),
Picasso96.

Installation: copy AAText to C: and add "Run >NIL: C:AAText" to
S:Startup-Sequence, after the monitor drivers and before LoadWB (not
WBStartup); copy AATextPrefs and its icon to SYS:Prefs for the
preferences program. See AAText_EN.txt
(English) or AAText_TR.txt (Turkish, ISO-8859-9) for details.

